.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH gpuq-hold 1  "gpuq 0.2.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
gpuq\-hold \- Hold a lease until Ctrl\-C
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgpuq hold\fR [\fB\-\-api\fR] [\fB\-\-class\fR] [\fB\-\-vram\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-card\fR] [\fB\-\-cards\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Hold a lease until Ctrl\-C
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-api\fR \fI<HOST:PORT>\fR
Address of the gpuq control API (default: $GPUQ_API, else 127.0.0.1:9390)
.TP
\fB\-\-class\fR \fI<CLASS>\fR [default: batch]
Priority class from gpuq\*(Aqs [classes] table
.TP
\fB\-\-vram\fR \fI<VRAM>\fR [default: all]
VRAM to reserve, e.g. 8G, 3000M or all
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR [default: manual]
Lease name shown in `gpuq status`
.TP
\fB\-\-card\fR \fI<NAME|LIST|all|any>\fR
Card to hold: a name from `gpuq status`, a comma list, `all` or `any`. Default: any card with room
.TP
\fB\-\-cards\fR \fI<N>\fR
Hold this many cards at once, any that have room
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgpuq\fR(1)
